# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal financial-data ignore rules.
#
# Enforced by tools/security_guards.py: every rule listed in that file's
# REQUIRED_IGNORE_RULES must still be present here, and no un-allowlisted
# negation (!pattern) may re-include one. .gitignore is order-sensitive, so a
# rule can be physically present yet no longer take effect.
#
# Default posture is privacy-first. This repository holds one person's whole
# balance sheet; everything that quotes an amount stays local. market/queries.json
# IS tracked on purpose -- it contains no personal data, it is small, and it is
# what makes a market claim replayable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- The financial position itself. Never commit these. -------------------
# Profile, balance sheet, holdings, risk profile: written by /setup.
profile/**
# Statements, payslips, broker exports the user drops in for /setup to read.
documents/**
!documents/README.md

# --- Market corpus: large and regenerable from market/queries.json --------
market/observations.json
market/evidence/**
market/snapshots/**
market/exports/**

# --- Decisions, advice, policy, actions, alerts, opinions -----------------
# Every one of these quotes real amounts against real accounts.
decision_tracker.csv
decisions/**
advice/**
ips/**
track/**
watch/**
views/**

# --- Refusal log ----------------------------------------------------------
# It quotes the text that was refused, which is the tip itself.
compliance/**

# --- Disposable and operational ------------------------------------------
.cache/**
.state/**
# State moved by /reset: never commit it on the way out either.
.reset-trash/

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# --- Tooling --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
